== Damage Scaling ==
Damage scaling is a mechanic introduced in [[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]] to provide a more challenging experience to players, enabling ''some'' enemies to retaliate against high damage attacks by deploying an "armor" of a sort to greatly reduce the amount of damage taken. Further details and an in-depth explanation may be found [[Damage Scaling|here]].

{{dlc|r+}} '''Satan''' has damage scaling.

== Notes ==
* Every time Satan is defeated, the current [[Savefile Images|savefile's image]] changes until {{i|The Negative}} is unlocked.
* Defeating Satan for the 1st time will unlock [[Champion]] versions of Bosses.
* Using the {{i|The Bible}} or {{p|XV - The Devil?}} on Satan will instantly kill Isaac.
* On the third wave, {{i|Pyromaniac}} and/or {{i|Host Hat}} will be extremely useful, as Kamikaze Leeches and stomping (which is considered as an explosion) will not hurt Isaac.
** {{dlc|r}} Stomps are no longer considered explosions and cannot have their damage negated.
* {{dlc|nr}} Unlike in the original ''Binding of Isaac'', Satan's feet don't cause damage on contact for the short time they rest on the ground after a stomp, providing a window of opportunity to deal significant damage with orbitals such as {{i|Sacrificial Dagger}}, or activate other contact effects like {{i|Midas' Touch}}.

== Trivia ==
* Satan appeared in the Halloween Update for the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
* Satan's pose as a statue and during the VS Screen is a nod to the demon [[Wikipedia:Baphomet|Baphomet]], who is usually portrayed in a similar pose.
* Satan, in mythology, began as a fallen angel but evolved over time into a greater evil. This may be the reason The Fallen spawns at the start of the fight, as well as the reason both of them have feathered wings.
* The demonic speech Satan shouts at the start of his first phase reuses one of Mom's voice lines, shouting "Isaac!" in reverse with heavy distortion.
* The [[music]] that plays during this battle is titled ''[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/track/hericide-satan-fight Hericide]''. Hericide is a combination of the latin word ''herus'' (or ''erus''), meaning master or lord, and the suffix -''cide'', denoting the act of killing.
* This song's melody shares some similarities with that of ''Periculum'', the [[Cellar]] theme. 
** This music also plays during the battle against {{e|Mega Satan}}.
** {{dlc|a}} This music also plays during the nightmare wave of [[Greed Mode]], for unlocking the floor's {{r|Devil Room}} or {{r|Angel Room}}.

